1.) Inbound Threat Detection (The Base Query)
This query isolates all failed RDP logon events to find exactly who is hitting your honeypot machine, extracting their IP addresses and account target names.

Code snippet
SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4625
| summarize FailedAttempts = count() by IpAddress, TargetUserName, Computer
| order by FailedAttempts desc



2.) Geolocation Aggregation (For Your Threat Map)
This query extracts the tracking data used to feed your visual Map Workbook, filtering out empty coordinates so they map flawlessly.

Code snippet
SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4625
| extend latitude = toreal(latitude), longitude = toreal(longitude)
| summarize FailedAttempts = count() by IpAddress, latitude, longitude, cityname, countryname
| where isnotempty(latitude) and isnotempty(longitude)



3.) Lateral Movement & Blast Radius Audit (Your Investigation Query)
This is the query you ran during your triage of Incident ID 5 to verify whether an attacker successfully breached the system or if they were completely deflected.

Code snippet
SecurityEvent
| where IpAddress == "103.93.36.129"
| where EventID in (4624, 4625)
| summarize Count = count() by EventID, Account
(Note: 4625 indicates a failed attempt, while 4624 indicates a successful logon.)



4.) High-Velocity Brute Force Threshold (Your Analytics Rule Logic)
This is the scheduled tracking query that automatically triggers your incidents when an attacker tries to log in too many times within a short window.

Code snippet
SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4625
| summarize FailedCount = count() by IpAddress, Account, Computer
| where FailedCount >= 10
